# Error pattern dictionaries

Add `{ message, category }` objects, not old string-map syntax:

```typescript
YOUR_ERROR_KEY: {
  message: "A friendly explanation and what to do.",
  category: "slippage",
},
```

- Put keys in the matching file: `evm.ts`, `solana.ts`, `tron.ts`, `ton.ts`, `sui.ts`, `btc.ts`, `wallets.ts`, `bridges.ts`, `generic.ts`, `swap-common.ts`.
- `src/data/error-map.ts` merges files, applies `CATEGORY_OVERRIDES`, and drops `DROPPED_KEYS` (`revert`, `reverted`, `GenericError`).
- No generic single-word substring keys (`revert`, `timeout`, `error`).
- Wrong-CTA categories to avoid: liquidity vs slippage; Tron energy is `gas`; Solana program errors are `contract_error`, not `wallet_connection`.
- Message: no jargon (`reverted`, `0x…`, `nonce`, `wei`), explain why, say what to do, one sentence, end with a period.
- Add a focused test in `src/matching.test.ts` or `src/patterns.test.ts` against `humanizeError` / `humanizeErrorDetailed` / `classifyError`.
